294	45,1268,435,1962 - 330,1740,435,1962	294. Flower, &c. of Frostweed.	A leafy stem of Frostweed topped by one open flower of five broad, crumpled petals round a tuft of many stamens, with a narrow leaf below.
295	340,1765,562,1972	295. Its calyx and pistil.	The calyx seen from above on its stalk: three large and two small pointed, hairy-edged sepals, with the short pistil standing in the centre.
296	462,1422,652,1712	296. Its ovary cut across and magnified.	The top of the ovary sliced off to show its one cell, with rows of small seeds borne on three parietal placentas projecting from the wall.
